{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>If silver.</b> It mentioned this commandment here because the poor man and the stranger and the orphan and the widow are equal in it." "<b>לא תהיה לו כנשה.</b> One may say it is an expression of forgetting, like 'כי נשני אלקים' (for Elohim has forgotten me). That is, do not be to him like one who has forgotten his loan and let a long time pass, in order to press him and take interest from him." "<b>לא תשימון עליו נשך.</b> To extend the time for him — five for six. <b>לא תשימון</b> is in plural language, for the borrower and the lender and the guarantor and the witnesses all transgress the negative commandment of לא תשימון."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:51.984318508Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}